# UI design specification

FRAMEWORK: Streamlit

PAGES:
- Starter: build a starterfile.pseudo section by section, then run the pipeline.
- Editor: create or edit pseudocode files and convert them to code.
- Converter: convert pseudocode to code (pseudo2code) and long notes to pseudocode (longtext2pseudo).
- Patcher: a context-aware chat that reads project files and proposes patches.

WORKFLOWS:
Starter has four tabs. Tab 1 edits # PATHS and # REPOMAP, tab 2 edits
# DATABASES, tab 3 edits # PSEUDOCODE, tab 4 reviews the assembled file and
runs the code_starter pipeline. Each of tabs 1-3 has a Verify button; on
success a Save button appears and the section is written into the starterfile.
Tab 4 runs the pipeline in the background and shows a per-stage report.

INPUTS AND OUTPUTS:
Project root and starterfile name are inputs. Editors are multi-line text
areas. Verification failures are shown as errors; successes as messages. The
pipeline report shows each stage pass/fail plus the smoke-test artifact.

VISUAL DESIGN:
A left sidebar lists the four pages. Wide layout, one primary column, tabs for
sub-sections, status messages inline.

ACCESSIBILITY:
Labels on every input, keyboard-navigable tabs, sufficient contrast.
